        "raw_text": "Momentum gap and go : exploring a stock trading strategy with statistical tools - Theseus Hyppää sisältöön Hae Theseuksesta Tämä kokoelma HAE Hakuohjeet JavaScript is disabled for your browser. Some features of this site may not work without it. Näytä viite Ammattikorkeakoulut Turun ammattikorkeakoulu Opinnäytetyöt (Avoin kokoelma) Näytä viite Ammattikorkeakoulut Turun ammattikorkeakoulu Opinnäytetyöt (Avoin kokoelma) Näytä viite Momentum gap and go : exploring a stock trading strategy with statistical tools Suomela, Dane (2024) Avaa tiedosto Suomela_Dane.pdf (730.7Kt) Lataukset: Suomela, Dane 2024 All rights reserved. This publication is copyrighted. You may download, display and print it for Your own personal use. Commercial use is prohibited. Näytä kaikki kuvailutiedot Julkaisun pysyvä osoite on https://urn.fi/URN:NBN:fi:amk-2024121335698 Tiivistelmä In the dynamic and unpredictable stock market, traders face the challenge of capitalizing on rapid price fluctuations. The Momentum Gap and Go strategy has gained prominence among day traders for targeting stocks with significant opening price gaps and high trading volumes. This study investigates the strategy's effectiveness, evaluating its potential profitability and identifying whether the strategy carries any merit. Using data from 374 small-cap stocks on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE) over a year, the research analyses stocks with price gaps of 20% or more under varying market conditions and gap sizes. Statistical methods, including correlation and cluster analyses, reveal key relationships between gap size, trading volume, and intraday profitability. Findings suggest smaller gaps (20%-50%) have the highest success rates, with bullish markets favoring specific long and short positions, while bearish markets generally benefit short-selling regardless of gap direction. The study underscores the strategy's potential for day traders. By providing actionable insights, this research contributes valuable knowledge to the evolving field of day trading strategies. Kokoelmat Opinnäytetyöt (Avoin kokoelma) Selaa kokoelmaa Nimekkeet Tekijät Julkaisuajat Koulutusalat Asiasanat Uusimmat Kokoelmat Henkilökunnalle",
