        "url": "https://github.com/bahramkhanlarov/Event-Based-Trading-Strategies-Exploiting-Earnings-Announcements",
        "raw_text": "GitHub - bahramkhanlarov/Event-Based-Trading-Strategies-Exploiting-Earnings-Announcements · GitHub Skip to content You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. Dismiss alert bahramkhanlarov / Event-Based-Trading-Strategies-Exploiting-Earnings-Announcements Public Notifications You must be signed in to change notification settings Fork 0 Star 4 main Branches Tags Go to file Code Open more actions menu Latest commit History 5 Commits 5 Commits Folders and files Name Name Last commit message Last commit date Event_Based_Trading_Strategies_Exploiting_Earnings_Announcements.ipynb Event_Based_Trading_Strategies_Exploiting_Earnings_Announcements.ipynb README.md README.md View all files Repository files navigation Event-Driven Stock Trading Strategy Based on Earnings Surprise This project implements an event-driven stock trading strategy that leverages earnings surprise to generate buy and sell signals. The strategy is designed to capitalize on the market's reaction to earnings announcements. Overview The core idea is that stocks tend to react positively when a company reports better-than-expected earnings (positive earnings surprise) and negatively when the earnings are worse than expected (negative earnings surprise). This strategy attempts to capture these price movements by taking a long position (buy) after positive surprises and a short position (sell) after negative surprises. Implemented Steps Data Fetching : Fetches historical stock prices and earnings data for a specified ticker (e.g., AAPL) using the yfinance library. Data Cleaning : Cleans and prepares the earnings data by converting date formats and resetting the index. Data Merging : Merges the price data and earnings data based on the date, aligning the earnings surprise with the corresponding stock price. Earnings Surprise Calculation : Calculates the earnings surprise by subtracting the estimated EPS from the reported EPS. Signal Generation : Generates trading signals based on the earnings surprise: 1 for positive surprise (buy) and -1 for negative surprise (sell). Strategy Simulation : Simulates the strategy by calculating returns for a defined holding period after each signal. Cumulative Return Calculation : Computes the cumulative return of the strategy over the entire period. Visualization : Plots the cumulative returns of the strategy over time. Libraries Used yfinance : For fetching stock data and earnings information. pandas : For data manipulation and analysis. numpy : For numerical computations. matplotlib : For plotting and data visualization. How to Run the Code Make sure you have the required libraries installed. You can install them using pip: Open the provided Python notebook in Google Colab or your local Jupyter environment. Execute the cells in the notebook to fetch data, calculate returns, and visualize the strategy performance. Strategy Parameters holding_period : The duration (in days) to hold a position after a signal is generated. It's set to 5 in the code, meaning the strategy will hold the position for 5 days. Key Concepts Earnings Surprise : The difference between a company's reported earnings per share (EPS) and the consensus analyst estimate of EPS. Event-Driven Strategy : A trading strategy that is triggered by specific events, such as earnings announcements. Potential Improvements Parameter Optimization : The holding period can be optimized to potentially enhance strategy performance. Transaction Costs : The simulation doesn't include transaction costs, which can significantly impact performance. Risk Management : Stop-loss and take-profit orders could be incorporated into the strategy. More Sophisticated Signals : More advanced methods of generating signals (e.g., using different thresholds for earnings surprise). Disclaimer This strategy is provided for educational purposes only and is not financial advice. The backtested performance is not indicative of future results. Trading involves risk, and you should conduct your own research before making any investment decisions. About No description, website, or topics provided. Resources Readme Activity Stars 4 stars Watchers 1 watching Forks 0 forks Report repository Releases Packages Contributors Languages You can’t perform that action at this time.",
